 "text": " What if a rock from space hit you during a map? November 30th, 1954, Silicauga, Alabama. Ann Hodges is asleep on her sofa under a quilt. A fireball streaks across three states. A black rock, four kilos, punches straight through her roof. It bounces off her radio and slams into her side. She wakes up with a huge bruise. By nightfall, 200 reporters are outside her house. The police take the rock. Then the Air Force takes it. Then her landlady sues. It landed on her house, she says, so it's hers. Anne pays her $500 and finally gets it back. The next day, a farmer finds a second piece lying in a dirt road. He sells it and buys a car and a house. Anne gives hers to a museum. To this day, she is the only person known to be hurt by a meteorite. Subscribe for more weird facts.",
